{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And if you say: What shall we eat in the seventh year</b> — this is inverted, as if to say: And if you say in the seventh year, 'What shall we eat?' — for their anxiety is on account of the eighth year, since the beginning of the shemittah year and the jubilee is from Tishrei. They will eat of the produce of the sixth year during the seventh year, according to the practice in all years, eating until after the harvest, which is at the festival of Shavuot, and even afterward until the work of the produce is completed — to winnow and to sift. Therefore the correct interpretation of \"and it shall yield produce for three years\" is with regard to the jubilee year: the sixth year will produce for the entire shemittah year and the jubilee and the year after the jubilee, for in all of them they will eat old grain. And Scripture promised: when you fear in the seventh year, saying, 'What shall we eat?' — I will command My blessing in the sixth year, so that it will yield produce for the three years that come after it, and it will be an added blessing sufficient even for the shemittah and the jubilee. And He said, \"and you shall sow the eighth year,\" to say that you shall sow in the eighth year according to the custom of the land, and you shall not rush to plow and to sow, nor to reap, for until its produce comes into the storehouse at the ingathering of the years, at the festival of Sukkot, you will eat old grain. And in Torat Kohanim (chapter 4:6): \"for three years\" — for the sixth and the seventh and the year after the shemittah. Another interpretation: \"for three years\" — for the seventh and the jubilee and the year after the jubilee."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The Hebrew מְסֹרָס (mesoras) means 'inverted' or 'transposed,' referring to the word order in the verse; rendered literally here. Torat Kohanim is Sifra, the halakhic midrash on Leviticus."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:00:17.186404732Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}